course: dictionary
lesson: 12895
title: Epithets: describing names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An epithet is a describing word or phrase added to a name. «Alfred the Great» is a name with an epithet: «the Great» tells you something about the king. Look for the extra words after the name.
explain: An epithet can also be a word used to describe someone, often an unkind one. If someone calls you a nasty name to hurt you, that name is an epithet, and it is not a kind one. Ask yourself: is this name a compliment or an insult?
explain: In stories and poems, an epithet is a short describing phrase that is used again and again, like «rosy-fingered dawn» in old Greek poems. When you spot one, ask: what picture does this phrase give me? It helps you see the character or place more clearly.
fact: An epithet is a describing word or phrase.
fact: «Alfred the Great» and «Richard the Lionheart» are names with epithets added.
fact: In history lessons, kings and queens often have epithets, such as «Ethelred the Unready».
fact: In old poems, a phrase such as «rosy-fingered dawn» is used again and again as an epithet.
fact: An epithet can be an insult, a nasty name used to describe someone.
exercise: «Alfred the Great ruled Wessex.» Which words are the epithet? | ruled | *the Great | Wessex | Alfred
exercise: «Olga the Bold led her men over the wall.» What does the epithet tell us? | Olga was very tall | Olga was ill that day | *Olga was brave | Olga lived by the sea
exercise: In an old poem: «The wine-dark sea rolled on.» What is «wine-dark sea»? | A type of boat | *A describing phrase used again and again | A sea song | A kind of drink
test: «Sam the Swift won the race.» Which word is the epithet? | Sam | race | *the Swift | won
test: Dan calls Mia «Lazy Lily» to hurt her feelings. What is this name? | A type of poem | *An epithet, an unkind name used to describe someone | A title for a king | A kind nickname
exam: «Richard the Lionheart fought in many battles.» What is the epithet? | battles | King | Richard | *the Lionheart
